  "details": "This has been a bug for a while and I was hoping it would be fixed with an update, but there is a reoccurring issue with sounds of all sorts that aren't voices. The sound effect or music or whatever it is can be heard for a split second when it's activated, no matter where you are on the map. Even using the VRC Spatial Audio in SDK2 does not fix this. I'm not sure if it's the audio file encoding or what, like often vorbis encoded sounds are fine especially when they are active on map load, but pcm and adpcm sounds almost always can be heard across the map briefly. (Could also be how they're streamed from memory? Maybe compressed in memory vs streamed from memory settings in the sounds?) I've also noticed when first loading into a map that has had audio triggered previously by someone else will often briefly play all the sounds that were triggered at once as the client loads trigger data, which can be really loud if it was a lot of them. \nAs an example, I'm currently using vrchat for a proof of concept of a game idea that has a steam ship with a telegraph. Whenever someone uses the telegraph, the first split second of the buzzing noise is heard everywhere, so if someone is pressing the button a lot, you will hear several buzzing noises almost every time. These sounds don't play on map load since it's not a trigger with a buffer, but other sounds that are on a buffered trigger will play when the map loads. Another example is I have a rather large map I'm working on and despite players being some 3,000 meters away from a sound source, they can still hear the first split second of the audio.\nTo me it seems that it's taking longer to load the settings of the audio source than the sound itself.",
